{
	"version": 5,
	"rows": [
		{
			"id": "eMn1QRTBuT8gYdY7x",
			"description": "Choppa",
			"local_notes": "Ork blades are all edge and mass, not balance; a choppa is never \"sharp\" in the fine sense, but a Boy's own strength does the real work.\n\nLore: The choppa is the other half of every Boy's standard loadout alongside the slugga: a heavy, crudely-forged cleaver, machete or cut-down sword welded from scrap and scavenged plate, and the single most common Ork melee weapon in Codex: Orks background, Deathwatch's Mark of the Xenos, and every piece of Ork army art the game has ever produced.\n\nDesign: Framework Ork anchor, revised after the combat simulator showed the old sw+3 cut could not get through flak 30 at all: a Boy's charge did no damage to a Guard line, against every depiction of Ork assaults. The choppa is now sw+1d(2) cut, the chainsword's divisor and one die less: the edge is crude, but a heavy scrap-steel cleaver swung by an Ork's strength splits flak plates the way a chainsword's teeth do. At a Boy's ST 22 (5d(2)) it penetrates flak (eff. 15) 69.5% of the time, carapace (eff. 35) never, and power armour never except at a Weak Point (1.6% of those); at a Nob's ST 26 (6d(2)) flak 90.4%, carapace still 0%. Power armour stays the job of the klaw and the big choppa's weight. Handling: weight 10 lb, min ST 11, skill Axe/Mace and parry -1U, as a crude, badly balanced cleaver.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Xenos",
				"Orks"
			],
