		{
			"id": "ee0pTiPLbzZ9a7jnW",
			"description": "Big Choppa",
			"local_notes": "A big two-handed cleaver, often favoured by Nobz who forgo a shield hand.\n\nLore: A two-handed, oversized choppa favoured by Nobz and mob bosses who want more reach and more raw hitting power than a one-handed choppa without going as far as a power klaw; a recurring silhouette in Codex: Orks Nob artwork and background, distinguished from the standard choppa mainly by size and the two-handed grip.\n\nDesign: One step up from the choppa, the same two-handed-over-one-handed step the Eviscerator takes over the chainsword: sw+2d(2) cut, two-handed, reach 1,2 (revised with the choppa after the combat simulator showed mundane Ork blades doing nothing to flak). At a Nob's ST 26 (7d(2)) it penetrates flak 97.8%, carapace 0.6%, and power armour only at a Weak Point, where it gets through 41% of the time: the one Ork blade short of a klaw that can open a Marine's armour at the seams.",
