		{
			"id": "eUKjB-yzNLFnqQr1k",
			"description": "Killsaw",
			"local_notes": "Cannot be used to Feint, as the Imperium Power Fist and Chainfist it's built from. Like the power klaw, the ring of chain-teeth carries a genuine (if crudely copied and worse-shielded) disruption field behind its spinning edge - Ork background is explicit that a killsaw bites through vehicle hulls and bulkheads the way a plain chain weapon never could, and this project models that with the same Armor Divisor every disruption-field weapon in this project shares, not with a bigger mundane blade. The teeth can still bind in a very solid hit exactly as an Imperium chainaxe's can (GM's discretion: a Ready maneuver to wrench it free).\n\nLore: A huge, motorised chain-blade mounted on a Meganob's arm alongside (or instead of) a power klaw, built for boarding actions and breaching where cutting through plate matters; Codex: Orks background places it as the Ork parallel to the Imperium chainfist, and is explicit that it genuinely cuts into tank hulls and bulkheads in the field - not merely a bigger version of a Boy-scale choppa's chain-teeth.\n\nDesign: Built on the Imperium Power Fist/Chainfist chassis (data/imperium/weapons/melee.yaml): thr+7d(10) cut, the Chainfist's own formula. Ork background is explicit that a killsaw cuts through tank hulls and bulkheads, which a mundane grinding chain with a small divisor (an earlier Armor Divisor (3) build reached only 0.1% against Astartes plate and essentially 0% against every vehicle AV) cannot do. It is reasoned as a crude, worse-shielded disruption field a Mek has copied or looted into the chain housing; the crudeness is carried in cost, upkeep and tone, not a weaker divisor, the same design choice this file makes for the Power Klaw against the Imperium Power Fist. Checked by exact dice distribution at the mega-armour-assisted strength a Meganob fights at (effective thrust around thr 3d+1, so thr+7d = 10d+1): avg 36, penetrating every personal armour on the table at or above 99.9%, including a Terminator, clearing AV10-12 essentially always, AV13 94.2% of the time and AV14 53.6% of the time, in line with the Astartes Chainfist's benchmark. Handling: 42 lb, and a cost well above a mundane chain weapon, in line with the Power Klaw's price jump over one; reach C, parry -2 and the no-Feint note are taken from the Imperium Power Fist/Chainfist, since a fist-and-forearm-mounted spinning ring fights like a servo-driven punching weapon, not a swung two-handed blade, which is also why the skill is Brawling. Min ST 22, reachable by mega armour's servo assistance or an unusually huge Ork, per the notes. TL 11 like the Imperial power weapons it copies; Meks build it by instinct (Mek Instinct offsets the TL penalties for them).",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Xenos",
				"Orks"
			],
			"tech_level": "11",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "6000",
			"base_weight": "42 lb",
			"weapons": [
