							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Brawling"
							}
						}
					]
				}
			],
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "eDzsU2cznCZ4M6Nxb",
			"description": "Power Klaw",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Ork answer to the power fist and the single most iconic Nob and Meganob weapon: a huge armoured gauntlet crackling with an unstable energy field, consistently shown across Codex: Orks background and Black Library Ork fiction crushing Space Marines, vehicle hulls and even Dreadnoughts one-handed - the framework's own anchor table cites it by name as \"like a power fist but cruder.\"\n\nDesign: Matches the framework's Ork anchor exactly (\"Power klaw | Power-field weapon: thr+8d(10) cr, like a power fist but cruder\"), built with the same first-principles logic as the Imperium Power Fist: the field's own servos generate most of the force, so the bonus is a large flat die addition to the wielder's own thrust (thr+8d) rather than a multiplier, and it shares the project's Armor Divisor (10) power-field rule. Checked by exact dice distribution at a mega-armoured Meganob's effective thrust (around thr 3d+1, giving thr+8d = 11d+1): avg 39.5, penetrating every personal armour on the table essentially always, including a Terminator (100%) - matching the anchor's own \"like a power fist ... kills Terminators\" reputation and the fiction's constant depiction of power klaws cracking open Dreadnoughts and Terminator squads alike. Even at a bare Boy's own strength (thr 2d, thr+8d=10d, avg 35) it still clears every personal armour at or above 99.7%, since the field itself - \"cruder\" than the Imperium version, per the anchor, but not meaningfully weaker in its actual armour- divisor effect - is doing almost all of the penetrating work regardless of who swings it. \"Cruder\" is modelled instead in cost, reliability and the entry's own tone rather than a lower divisor, since dropping the divisor below (10) would break the anchor's own explicit \"like a power fist\" equivalence. TL 11 like the Imperium Power Fist (framework TL table: power weapons 11); Meks build the klaw by instinct, so Mek Instinct offsets the TL penalty for them, not a lowered TL. Handling: 45 lb, matching the Imperium Power Fist's own weight class for a similarly huge servo-driven gauntlet; min ST 22 (a Boy's own strength, though in practice almost always a Nob or Meganob wears one, per the framework's \"built for Ork hands\" convention). Reach C, parry -2 and the no-Feint note directly mirror the Imperium Power Fist's own handling rules, since both weapons share the same \"huge servo-fist, slow to reposition\" fighting style.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Xenos",
				"Orks"
			],
			"tech_level": "11",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "9000",
			"base_weight": "45 lb",
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "whkUapa7A_lmt5krd",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "cr",
						"st": "thr",
						"base": "8d",
						"armor_divisor": 10
					},
					"reach": "C",
					"parry": "-2",
					"strength": "22",
					"usage": "Punch/crush",
					"usage_notes": "Cannot be used to Feint, as the Imperium power fist it's built from. The field is a genuine disruption field (built, per Ork fashion, by copying or looting the principle rather than understanding it) and shares the project's power-field Armor Divisor (10).",
					"defaults": [
						{
							"type": "dx",
							"modifier": 0
						},
						{
							"type": "skill",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Brawling"
							}
						}
					]
				}
			],
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "eiTz3ARSTlpLKR8HB",
			"description": "Power Stabba",
			"local_notes": "Field toggle as the Imperium Power Sword family; a depleted or crudely-wired cell disables the field the same way.\n\nLore: A rarer, thrusting cousin of the power klaw - a heavy iron stake or spike wrapped in the same crude field generator - favoured by Nobz who want to punch through a target rather than crush it; less iconic than the power klaw but recurring in Ork background as an alternative Nob power weapon.\n\nDesign: Applies this project's power-field rule (framework.md: +3d damage, Armor Divisor (10), field on vs. off) to a plain heavy iron stake's mundane baseline (thr+2 imp, one step above a bare thrusting spike for the sheer mass of Ork ironwork) rather than to the power klaw's own crushing baseline, since a stabbing spike and a crushing gauntlet are not the same mundane weapon with a field bolted on. Checked by exact dice distribution at a Nob's own strength (thr approx. 2d+1, so field on totals thr+2+3d = 5d+3): avg 20.5, penetrating every personal armour at or above 99.7% up to Astartes power armour, and 50.0% of the time even against a Terminator - a genuinely dangerous power weapon in a Nob's hands, on the same tier as the Imperium's own human-scale Power Sword against comparable armour, matching its place as a real but secondary alternative to the power klaw. Handling: 20 lb (lighter than the Power Klaw's 45 lb - a spike and generator, not a full gauntlet), min ST 18 (a Nob manages it readily; a Boy struggles), Spear skill and reach 1 for a thrusting weapon, parry -1U matching the Imperium Power Lance's own crude, hard-to-recover braced-spear convention. TL 11 like the Imperium power weapons (framework TL table); Mek Instinct offsets the TL penalty for the Meks who build it.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Xenos",
				"Orks"
			],
