		{
			"id": "eau_fNFqbjf0CojNS",
			"description": "Mek's Kustom Tools",
			"local_notes": "Represents the whole belt of tools (big wrenches, welding clamps, choppy screwdrivers) a Mek carries rather than a single named item; a Mek wielding these in combat is understood to be improvising, not fighting with purpose-built wargear. When actually used for their intended job, this item gives no combat bonus but is required kit for any Engineer/Mechanic (Ork Tech) work a Mek attempts in the field.\n\nLore: Every Mekboy carries a belt or backpack of oversized, improvised tools - the same kit that builds and repairs Ork vehicles and wargear - and Ork background consistently shows Meks swinging a big wrench or cutting torch on anyone who gets between them and their latest project as readily as any Boy swings a choppa.\n\nDesign: Not a weapon anchor; built as a generic heavy improvised tool on the same Basic Set logic as the Imperium Entrenching Tool (sw+1 cr, reach 1, parry -1U, Axe/Mace) rather than inventing a dedicated Mek melee weapon, since the fiction treats a Mek's tools as exactly that - tools pressed into service, not wargear. Handling: 15 lb for the practical weight of \"a belt of Mek-scale tools,\" heavier than the Imperium Entrenching Tool (5 lb) for the sheer bulk a Mekboy hauls around; min ST 11, trivial for any Ork. The item's real value at the table is as the required equipment tag for a Mek's Engineer/Mechanic (Ork Tech) work (see framework.md's skills table: \"Mekboyz build by instinct... a genetic Talent for Engineer/Mechanic/Armoury\"), with the melee profile included for completeness rather than as the item's main purpose.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Xenos",
				"Orks"
			],
			"tech_level": "6",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "200",
			"base_weight": "15 lb",
