		{
			"id": "eX5EUY22a0OVnQVps",
			"description": "Weirdboy Staff",
			"local_notes": "Mechanically a plain quarterstaff. Ork lore holds that a Weirdboy's staff channels and focuses his psychic power (fed by nearby Orks' WAAAGH! energy, per framework.md's Ork psychic note), and background art always shows Weirdboyz carrying one crackling with barely restrained energy - but any actual psychic power the Weirdboy wields belongs to that psyker's own traits and powers (built on this project's Thaumatology: Sorcery chassis, see framework.md's Psykers and the Warp section), not to the staff itself. A GM wanting a staff that visibly arcs or sparks in a Weirdboy's hands is encouraged to treat that as pure colour tied to the wielder's own power, exactly as the framework already handles the Imperium Power Stave versus a psyker's force stave.\n\nLore: Every Weirdboy is depicted carrying a tall, gnarled or scrap-metal staff, often topped with a skull or crude glyphs, that background material (Codex: Orks) treats as a focus for the Weirdboy's own barely-controlled psychic power rather than as a weapon in its own right - Weirdboyz are dangerous for what they can do with the WAAAGH!, not for how hard they can hit with a stick.\n\nDesign: Deliberately statted as a mundane quarterstaff (sw+1 cr/thr+1 cr, reach 1,2, parry 0, Staff skill), the same \"mundane object, psychic power belongs elsewhere\" logic this project already applies to the Imperium Power Stave versus a force stave (see the Imperium melee file): nothing in Ork background describes the staff itself doing anything a plain stick couldn't, and giving it a bespoke mechanical effect would invent a psychic-power interaction the framework's own Psykers and the Warp section doesn't support for this project's Ork material. Handling: 6 lb and min ST 10 are ordinary Basic Set quarterstaff figures; Staff's own built-in defensive bonus (parry 0, no U) is unchanged from every other staff-family entry in this project.",
